Data Sources and References

This file documents the datasets and public information sources identified for the project *Agricultural Market Price Trend Analysis and Forecasting Using Indian Mandi Data*.

1. Primary Dataset

Dataset Name: Daily Commodity Prices India

Platform: Kaggle

Dataset URL: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/khandelwalmanas/daily-commodity-prices-india

Purpose: This dataset is the primary source for analyzing historical agricultural commodity market prices in India. It will be inspected to identify available price fields, dates, commodities, and market locations.

 2. Additional Public Data Sources

AGMARKNET
URL: https://agmarknet.gov.in/

Purpose: Agricultural marketing information, including mandi market prices and related market information.

 Open Government Data Platform India
URL: https://www.data.gov.in/

Purpose: Identify supplementary government datasets related to agricultural markets, commodities, and production.

 Directorate of Economics and Statistics
URL: https://desagri.gov.in/

Purpose: Potential supplementary source for agricultural production, area, and yield statistics if the project scope expands beyond price analysis.

India Meteorological Department
URL: https://mausam.imd.gov.in/

Purpose: Potential source for weather and rainfall information if a separate analysis of weather and agricultural market trends is undertaken.

3. Planned Use of Sources

The Kaggle dataset will be the primary dataset for the project. Additional sources will be consulted only when required for supplementary analysis or verification.

The planned analysis includes:
- Historical commodity price trends
- Minimum, maximum, and modal price comparisons
- Price fluctuations and percentage changes
- Comparisons across selected markets and commodities
- Exploratory forecasting for a selected commodity-market series, if suitable data is available

4. Data Usage and Attribution

Before downloading, using, or redistributing any dataset, review its licence, terms of use, and attribution requirements. Dataset fields, coverage, units, and source metadata should be verified before analysis.

Project status: Sources identified during the planning stage. Their use and suitability will be confirmed as the project progresses.

